  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Chip Filter Search\r\n\r\nYour goal is to finish and test a **chip-based search** that helps students quickly find study resources by clicking on tag chips (like “quadratics,” “civil rights,” or “coding”). The function should:\r\n\r\n- Take `data` and a `tag` value (from the chip the user clicked).\r\n- Trim extra spaces from the tag.\r\n- Compare strings in a **case-insensitive** way.\r\n- Show **all resources** when the “All” chip is selected.\r\n- Skip resources that are missing a `tags` list.\r\n- Not change the original dataset.\r\n\r\n::: details [Steps]\r\n\r\n1. In `script.js`, find the `searchByChip(data, tag)` function.\r\n\r\n2. Use the AI helper (CHAT Co-Build):\r\n   - Paste just this function into the chat.\r\n   - Use the C–H–A–T structure:\r\n     - **Clarify**: Ask AI to restate what the function should do with `data` and `tag`, and how it affects what shows in the results area (the list of study resources and match counts).\r\n     - **Hone**: Ask for help adding:\r\n       - `trim()` to clean the tag.\r\n       - Lowercasing on both sides before comparing.\r\n       - A guard so resources missing a `tags` array are skipped safely.\r\n       - A check so that when the chip `\"All\"` is clicked, **all resources** are shown.\r\n\r\n3. **Apply**  \r\n   Implement or refine the function based on the AI’s suggestions:\r\n   - Build a `results` array.\r\n   - Normalize the clicked tag.\r\n   - If the tag is `\"all\"`, return a **copy** of all resources.\r\n   - Otherwise, use `.map()` to examine each resource.\r\n   - For each resource:\r\n     - Safely read its `tags` array.\r\n     - Normalize each tag.\r\n     - Check whether the item includes the selected tag.\r\n     - If it does, add it to `results`.\r\n\r\n4. Test Cases for the Study Hub:\r\n   - **Mixed case**: click a chip and ensure matches work even if the resource tags have different capitalization (e.g., “Coding” vs “coding”).\r\n   - **All chip**: click “All” and confirm all resources appear again.\r\n   - **Chip with 0 results**: click a tag that does not exist in the dataset (add a temporary chip to try this), and confirm it shows “0” matches.\r\n   - **Whitespace test**: simulate a chip containing extra spaces (e.g., `\"  math  \"`), and confirm search still works.\r\n\r\n5. In the backpack, save a reusable prompt **Template** you might use in the future, with placeholders like `{data}`, `{tag}`, and `{targetChip}` for chip-based searches across different types of datasets.\r\n\r\n:::",
    "submittable": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
    "widget_view": "false",
    "initial_view_mode": "split",
    "ai_tutor_mode": "engineer",
    "predict_settings": {
